port."]}],["$","p","12",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- 68% of major ISPs (including Gmail, Outlook.com, and Apple Mail) now use *authentication signals as primary trust indicators*, superseding sender reputation alone."]}],["$","p","13",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Phishing attacks leveraging unauthenticated domains rose ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"31% YoY in 2025"}],", accelerating stricter enforcement."]}],["$","p","15",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Authentication isn't optional--it's your digital \"passport\" for email. Let's configure it correctly."]}],["$","hr","17",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","h2","19",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Step 1: SPF (Sender Policy Framework) -- Define *Who Can Send*"}],["$","p","21",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["SPF tells receiving servers which IP addresses and domains are authorized to send email *on behalf of your domain*."]}],["$","h3","23",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"✅ Best Practices for 2026:"}],["$","p","24",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Use `include:` only for *verified, maintained* third-party services (e.g., `include:sendgrid.net`, `include:mailchimp.com`)."]}],["$","p","25",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Never exceed 10 DNS lookups"}]," -- each `include`, `a`, or `mx` record counts. Exceeding this causes SPF \"permerror\" (treated as *fail*)."]}],"$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31",