19:["$","p","26",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Avoid `+all` -- it's insecure and deprecated. Use `-all` (hard fail) instead."]}]
1a:["$","h3","28",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"🔧 Configuration Example:"}]
1b:["$","p","29",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```text"]}]
1c:["$","p","30",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["example.com.  IN  TXT  \"v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com include:sendgrid.net ip4:203.0.113.42 -all\""]}]
1d:["$","p","31",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```"]}]
1e:["$","p","33",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> 💡 ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Actionable Tip"}],": Run `dig txt example.com` or use [MXToolbox SPF Lookup](https://mxtoolbox.com/spf.aspx) to verify syntax and lookup count. If you're using 3+ ESPs (e.g., HubSpot + Mailgun + internal SMTP), consolidate via a *dedicated subdomain* (e.g., `news.example.com`) for marketing mail -- simplifies SPF and improves reputation segmentation."]}]
1f:["$","hr","35",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}]
20:["$","h2","37",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Step 2: DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) -- Prove *Email Integrity*"}]
21:["$","p","39",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["DKIM adds a cryptographic signature to every outgoing email, verifying that the message wasn't altered in transit and truly originated from your domain."]}]
22:["$","h3","41",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"✅ Best Practices for 2026:"}]
23:["$","p","42",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Use ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"RSA 2048-bit keys minimum"}]," (1024-bit is deprecated and rejected by Apple Mail as of Q1 2026)."]}]
24:["$","p","43",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Rotate DKIM keys ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"every 6-12 months"}],", especially after vendor changes or security incidents."]}]
25:["$","p","44",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Sign *all* sending domains -- including transactional (`auth.example.com`) and marketing (`news.example.com`) subdomains."]}]
26:["$","h3","46",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"🔧 Setup Workflow:"}]
27:["$","p","47",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["1. Generate a 2048-bit key pair (use OpenSSL or your ESP's UI)."]}]
28:["$","p","48",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["2. Publish the public key in DNS as a TXT record at `selector._domainkey.example.com`."]}]
29:["$","p","49",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["3. Configure your email platform to sign with the private key."]}]
2a:["$","h3","51",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"Example DNS Record (Selector: `s2026`):"}]
2b:["$","p","52",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```text"]}]
2c:["$","p","53",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["s2026._domainkey.example.com.  IN  TXT  \"v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQC...[truncated 344-char base64]\""]}]
2d:["$","p","54",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```"]}]
2e:["$","p","56",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> 💡 ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Actionable Tip"}],": Test signatures in real time using [DKIM Validator](https://dkimvalidator.com/) -- send a test email and paste headers. Look for `dkim=pass` and `arc=pass` in Gmail's \"Show original\" view. *No pass = no inbox.*"]}]
2f:["$","hr","58",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}]
30:["$","h2","60",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"Step 3: DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting & Conformance) -- Enforce & Monitor"}]
31:["$","p","62",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["DMARC ties SPF and DKIM together and tells receivers what to do when authentication fails -- plus delivers forensic reports."]}]
32:["$","h3","64",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"✅ Critical 2026 Requirements:"}]
33:["$","p","65",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"`p=none` is no longer safe"}],": As of Jan 2026, Google and Yahoo require `p=quarantine` (for new senders) or `p=reject` (for established bulk senders ≥5k emails/month)."]}]
34:["$","p","66",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Publish `rua` and `ruf` tags"}],": You *must* collect aggregate (`rua`) and forensic (`ruf`) reports to troubleshoot."]}]
35:["$","p","67",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Use subdomain policies"}],": Apply strict `p=reject` to `example.com`, but looser `p=quarantine` to `legacy.example.com` during migration."]}]
36:["$","h3","69",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"🔧 Minimum Viable DMARC Record (2026 Compliant):"}]
37:["$","p","70",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```text"]}]
38:["$","p","71",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["_dmarc.example.com.  IN  TXT  \"v=DMARC1; p=reject; rua=mailto:dmarc-reports@example.com; ruf=mailto:forensic@example.com; fo=1; adkim=s; aspf=s\""]}]
39:["$","p","72",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["```"]}]
3a:["$","p","74",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- `fo=1`: Generate reports on *any* authentication failure (SPF *or* DKIM)."]}]
3b:["$","p","75",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- `adkim=s` / `aspf=s`: Enforce *strict* alignment (subdomain must match exactly -- e.g., `news.example.com` sending requires `news.example.com` in DKIM `d=` and SPF `Return-Path`)."]}]
3c:["$","p","76",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- `ri=86400`: Reports every 24 hours (default -- recommended)."]}]
3d:["$","p","78",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> 💡 ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Actionable Tip"}],": Start with `p=none` *only if you've never collected reports before*. Analyze 7 days of `rua` reports (use free tools like [Postmark DMARC Analyzer](https://dmarc.postmarkapp.com/) or [Valimail Dashboard](https://www.valimail.com/)), then move to `p=quarantine` → `p=reject` within 14 days. *Delaying enforcement risks blacklisting.*"]}]
